{
  "correction_rules": [
    "Persistent low bias across the full 30D horizon: model underpredicts levels by ~+6 to +10 €/t on average; apply an upward level shift, larger in the first ~20 days.",
    "Trend/acceleration lag in rising markets: when the last 10–15 days show a strong upswing, the model projects flattening/mean-reversion too early; add a positive trend term proportional to recent slope (e.g., +0.3 to +0.6 × 10D slope) for days 1–15.",
    "Mid-horizon underestimation of peaks: true path often continues to higher highs (around days ~8–22) while forecast stays capped in low/mid-70s; increase convexity (allow higher peak) when recent volatility + momentum are high.",
    "Late-horizon direction error: model often stays too high late (days ~25–30) when the true series rolls over; apply mild downward adjustment in the last week if the forecast is still rising/flat while recent momentum has weakened.",
    "Volatility compression: forecast range is too narrow versus realized swings; widen forecast dispersion by scaling deviations from the mean (e.g., multiply anomalies by ~1.2–1.4) during high-momentum regimes."
  ]
}
